# TRE version taxonomy — end-to-end inventory

Magic at bytes 0..3 is always `EERT` (`0x45 0x45 0x52 0x54`) on read and write (`TreArchive.cpp:145-149`, `TreBuilder.cpp:152-153`).

---

## 1. Per-arm taxonomy table

| Arm | (a) READ bytes @4..7 → arm | (b) WRITE bytes @0..7 | Stride | `isCrcFirst(v)` | `isEnumerateOnly(v)` | Codec (read payload) | Codec (write payload) | Codec (TOC/name read/write) | Build/repack | Other version-keyed behavior |
|-----|------------------------------|-------------------------|--------|-----------------|----------------------|----------------------|----------------------|----------------------------|--------------|------------------------------|
| **V0004** | ASCII `0004` (`0x30×3 + 0x34`) via `parseVersionString` @ `TreVersion.h:58` | `EERT` + `0004` @ `TreBuilder.cpp:152-166` | 24 @ `TreVersion.h:82` | `true` (unused in parser) @ `TreVersion.h:106-108` | `false` @ `TreVersion.h:123-125` | `codecForCompressor(entry.compressor)` → 0=`StoredCodec`, else `ZlibCodec` @ `TreCodec.cpp:35-46`, `TreArchive.cpp:363-365` | `codecForTreVersion(version)` → always `ZlibCodec` (version ignored) @ `TreCodec.cpp:48-52`, `TreBuilder.cpp:257` | `codecForBlockCompressor(tocCompressor/blockCompressor)` @ `TreArchive.cpp:194-196`, `217-220`, `TreBuilder.cpp:323`, `349` | Allowed | UI label `v0004` @ `TreMount.cpp:28` |
| **V0005** | ASCII `0005` @ `TreVersion.h:59` | `EERT` + `0005` @ `TreBuilder.cpp:160`, **binding default** @ `tre_binding.cpp:818`, `944` | 24 @ `TreVersion.h:83` | `true` (unused) | `false` | Same as V0004 | Same as V0004 | Same as V0004 | Allowed; **default** when version arg omitted or unparseable @ `tre_binding.cpp:818-822`, `944-948` | Dominant test/build default (`tre-builder-roundtrip.test.ts:126-130`) |
| **V0006** | ASCII `0006` @ `TreVersion.h:60` | `EERT` + `0006` @ `TreBuilder.cpp:161` | 24 @ `TreVersion.h:84` | `true` (unused) | `false` @ `TreVersion.h:114-115` | Same as V0004 | Same as V0004 | Same as V0004 | Allowed | Docs/contracts: readable, not encrypted @ `contracts/src/tre.ts:51-52` |
| **V5000** | ASCII `5000` @ `TreVersion.h:61` | `EERT` + `5000` @ `TreBuilder.cpp:162` | 24 @ `TreVersion.h:85` | `true` (unused) | `false` | Same as V0004 | Same as V0004 | Same as V0004 | Allowed; **deploy path** @ `packPatch.ts:116` | Retail stock tag for many clients (e.g. `bottom.tre`) @ `TreVersion.h:15-16`, `docs/01-core-engine/iff-and-tre.md:308-309` |
| **V6000** | ASCII `6000` @ `TreVersion.h:62` | `EERT` + `6000` @ `TreBuilder.cpp:163` (only if build were allowed) | **32** (+8 zero pad @ TOC `[24..31]`) @ `TreVersion.h:86`, `TreBuilder.cpp:313`, `TreArchive.cpp:261` | `true` (unused) | **`true`** @ `TreVersion.h:123-125` | Same codec seam; **no decryption** — encrypted payloads fail inflate / length gate @ `TreArchive.cpp:418-437` | **`TreBuilder::build/repack` throws** before codec @ `TreBuilder.cpp:187-191`, `392-395` | Same as V0004 for blocks that parse | **Refused** (write/repack) | `getMountArchives().enumerateOnly = true` @ `TreMount.cpp:345`; extract via internal TOC **not** version-blocked @ `TreArchive.cpp:319-329`; empty-TOC containers use `extractAt` + master `.toc` @ `tre_binding.cpp:1371-1374` |

### Parse sites (READ @4..7)

| Site | Behavior |
|------|----------|
| `parseVersionString(const char[4])` | Only site that maps bytes → enum; `memcmp` on `"0004"`…`"6000"`; else throws @ `TreVersion.h:57-66` |
| `TreArchive::parse` | Reads 36-byte header; calls `parseVersionString(hdr+4)` @ `TreArchive.cpp:154` |
| N-API `BuildTre` / `RepackTre` | Optional JS string → `parseVersionString(vstr.c_str())`; **invalid string silently keeps `V0005`** (`catch (...) {}`) @ `tre_binding.cpp:818-822`, `944-948` |

### Write sites (header @0..7)

| Site | Behavior |
|------|----------|
| `TreBuilder::writeHeader` | Writes `EERT` + 4-char version switch @ `TreBuilder.cpp:152-166`; re-written at end @ `TreBuilder.cpp:376-377` |
| `scripts/generate-tre-fixtures.js` `buildHeader` | Same pattern @ `generate-tre-fixtures.js:76-87` |

### `isCrcFirst` — defined but not wired

- Declared: always returns `true` @ `TreVersion.h:106-108`.
- **No C++ call sites** under `packages/native-core` (parser is unconditionally crc-first @ `TreArchive.cpp:224-248`).
- **Neutral disagreement:** `packages/harness/fixtures-real/README.md:21` claims `isCrcFirst(V0005)` returns `false`; code returns `true`.

---

## 2. `buildTre` / `repackTre` callers and version argument

| Caller | Location | Version passed |
|--------|----------|----------------|
| N-API default | `tre_binding.cpp:818`, `944` | **`V0005`** if arg omitted |
| N-API invalid string | `tre_binding.cpp:821`, `947` | Silent fallback **`V0005`** |
| `packPatch` (production deploy) | `packPatch.ts:116` | **`'5000'`** explicit |
| `tre-codec.test.ts` | `:106-107`, `:147`, `:177`, `:181`, `:212` | `'0005'`; repack no version → default; `'6000'` expect throw |
| `packPatch.test.ts` | `:47`, `:68`, `:82`, `:118-119` | `'5000'` / `'0005'` |
| `patch-shadow.test.ts` | `:57`, `:63`, `:89`, `:95` | **`'5000'`** |
| `tre-builder-roundtrip.test.ts` | `:70`, `:98`, etc. | **Omitted → `V0005`** |
| `tre-retail-repack.test.ts` | `:118`, `:123`, `:166`, `:180`, `:218`, `:222`, `:237` | Omitted except `'6000'` throw test; **real repack does not pass source version** |
| C++ `TreBuilder::build` | `TreBuilder.cpp:181-183` | From caller enum |
| C++ `TreBuilder::repack` | `TreBuilder.cpp:390`, `462` | From caller enum; **does not copy source `TreArchive::version()`** |

**Note:** `repackTre(path)` on a retail `EERT5000` archive without 3rd arg emits **`EERT0005`** in the output header (binding default).

---

## 3. Version strings in UI / persisted state

| Surface | Source | Format user sees | Retail example |
|---------|--------|------------------|----------------|
| Native `getMountArchives` | `TreMount.cpp:26-34`, `344` | `"v0004"`…`"v6000"` | From on-disk tag |
| `treMount.ts` → `MountedArchive.version` | `treMount.ts:44-49`, `171`, `308` | Same union; unknown → **`v0005` fallback** | |
| `MountedArchivesList` version chip | `MountedArchivesList.tsx:118-132` | Renders `archive.version` | Stock `bottom.tre`: **`v5000`**; Restoration: **`v6000`** |
| `ProjectBindingBar` TRE chip | `ProjectBindingBar.tsx:106-107` | First mounted archive, **`v` stripped** (`5000`, `6000`, …) | |
| `treStore.MountedArchive` | `treStore.ts:30-31` | Persisted in Zustand for session | |
| `MountArchiveAsync` result | `tre_binding.cpp:638`, `656-664` | `"vNNNN"` on async single mount | |
| Deploy output | `packPatch.ts` | File on disk **`EERT5000`**; UI shows mounted archives’ native tags, not patch file until mounted | |
| Project / workspace JSON | No TRE version field found in binding metadata | N/A | |

**Enumerate-only chip (separate from version chip):** starts `false` @ `treMount.ts:174`, `311`; set by `markArchiveEncrypted` on `extractMountAt` failure @ `treStore.ts:273-278`; label `≈ enumerate-only (encrypted)` @ `MountedArchivesList.tsx:141-156`.

**Neutral disagreement:** native `getMountArchives` exposes `enumerateOnly: isEnumerateOnly(ver)` @ `TreMount.cpp:345`, but renderer **overwrites to `false` at mount** @ `treMount.ts:174`.

