### Committed fixture header bytes (`scripts/generate-tre-fixtures.js`)

| File | @0..3 | @4..7 | Stride | Notes |
|------|-------|-------|--------|-------|
| `v0005-3record.tre` | `EERT` | `0005` | 24 | @ `:116` |
| `v0006-2record.tre` | `EERT` | `0006` | 24 | @ `:140` |
| `v6000-2record.tre` | `EERT` | `6000` | 32 | @ `:181`; stored payloads, compressor 0 |
| `malformed-magic.tre` | `TREE` | `0005` | — | @ `:189-190` |
| `truncated.tre` | `EERT` | `0005` | — | @ `:196` |
| `unsupported-version.tre` | `EERT` | `9999` | — | @ `:203-204` |
| `malformed-bad-adler.tre` | `EERT` | `0005` | 24 | @ `:233` |
| `crc-collision.tre` | `EERT` | `0005` | 24 | @ `:258` |
| `v6000-encrypted.tre` | (committed; **not** in generator `@:263-272`) | `6000` (per tests) | 32 | Used by roundtrip/async/codec tests |

**TreBuilder vs external reader:** No test byte-compares a **fresh `buildTre` output** to a **retail** archive. Closest external checks: field-order arbiter on real reads, retail repack **decompressed payload** equality, v6000 sidecar zlib oracles.

